  "agent": "Better Properties North Proctor",
  "text": "This solid 1904 Craftsman home features 4 bedrooms and 2.5 bathrooms. It is located in the popular Minor neighborhood in Central Seattle. The lower level has it's own separate entrance to a wonderfully furnished one-bedroom ADU with a full bathroom. Property updates include: new siding, paint, windows, solar panels, front porch, back deck, & newly lined sewer pipe. Original charm is evident throughout to include: stately entry with period staircase, original doorknobs, pocket door in living room, fir floors on the main & upper level, 5 panel doors, & exposed beams. This well laid out, bright, and clean home has a wonderful downtown view which is especially beautiful at night. The home is largely turnkey and un-updated, it is ready for your personal upgrades without having to worry about major system upgrades or expensive repairs. The home is three levels and is situated on a 4,000 square ft lot, with a private backyard which is level and includes a newer deck. It is located on a tree lined street with sidewalks and landscaped roundabouts in one of Seattle's most vibrant and evolving neighborhoods. Living here you will be close to some of the city's best restaurants, coffee shops, parks, neighborhood favorites, and everything the Central District has to offer. Whether you're heading downtown, over to Capitol Hill, or simply enjoying the neighborhood, this is an ideal home location. Proximity to hospitals is another marked benefit along with the highly rated public schools.",
